  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Congregational hymn singing of the Laestadian revival begun in the mid-nineteenth century by the Swedish pastor Lars Levi Laestadius in Karesuando and Pajala, which spread through Swedish and Finnish Tornedalen, northern Norway and Ostrobothnia. Its songbooks, Sions sånger in Swedish and Siionin laulut in Finnish, are sung at seurat prayer meetings in prayer houses, and Svenskt visarkiv has recorded the orally carried tunes of tradition-bearers in northern Sweden.",
